# Checkout kernel

**Invariant:** `¬attribute(path, this_session ∨ this_dispatch) ⇒ ¬delete(path) ∧ ¬revert(path)`.
On sole shared `master` (Lane A) untracked / dirty / "noise" is usually **parallel WIP**. `??`, same-mtime,
absent-from-`files_expected`, `status=partial` are not authorship. Cannot trace origin ⇒ leave + flag; ask
before delete; delete only when proven yours or operator-directed. Lane-B worktrees (`cursor-sdk/lane-{thread}`)
get the same rule.

## Vocabulary

`commit` = repository checkpoint, not activation, **not a human permission gate** (never "waiting
to be asked to commit"). On work_complete it is a required finishing act.
`deploy` = propagate a tree/commit identity. `activate` / `go live` = finish: land → path-explicit
commit of session paths → recycle every serving process + graph stamp (`restart-drain-discipline`).
Recycle-from-dirty-tree is exceptional, not the ordinary-live default; `live@sha` is already
commit-then-recycle. Liveness proof is `fleet_liveness(code_ref=…)`;
repo timestamps / `recent_commits` are low-confidence fallback.

`land(lane_B) ⇒ git merge cursor-sdk/lane-{thread}` — `checkout <branch> -- <paths>` and `cherry-pick` are
**copies, not lands**: they clobber dirty peer WIP with no conflict and leave the branch unmerged (branch debt
on shipped work). `dirty ∩ incoming ⇒ commit overlapping ≺ merge` and resolve keep-both. **¬ stash**
instead of merge; **¬ leave a stash unpopped**. `merge_blocked ⇒ reconcile`, never route around git;
`git_land` is `arc/*`-only. Bind a:29557.

## Lanes

Attended IDE = live shared checkout. `cursor-sdk` generate: pass `lane="B"` for every top-level admit, including a cortex-only spec. A throwaway worktree is enough. Omit is
**not** Lane B (empty `files_expected` + omit → Lane A). Lane A is one write slot; a seat does not raise that cap or pass `lane="A"` to avoid a tree. `lane="A"` only when lane B is refused for paths outside the repo. Lane A: no
intersecting parallel writers, no `git stash` to isolate or A/B against HEAD — read the tree. IDE hygiene:
commit this-session paths often or dispatch new implement on B; do not remint A-authored dirt onto B.

## Personal vs public

`personal_life(helper ∨ workflow) ⇒ ¬track(public_remote) ∧ track(nested_git under *.local/)` — `scripts.local/`,
`{satellite}/scripts.local/`, `tools/local/`, `pipelines.local/`; life skills/rules ignored in place. Never
name an employer or matter in a `_ws`/`_ulg` rule; never bake personal defaults into public CLIs.

